{"id":"b9","level":3,"levelName":"Ulpan Bet","n":9,"of":9,"title":"Saying no","titleHe":"שְׁלִילָה","goal":"Negate a verb, an existence, and a whole idea.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"לֹא goes before the verb and negates it. אֵין negates existence. They aren't interchangeable: אֲנִי לֹא רוֹאֶה is I don't see, but אֵין סֵפֶר is there's no book."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אֲנִי לֹא יוֹדֵעַ.","en":"I don't know."},{"he":"אֵין לִי כֶּסֶף.","en":"I have no money."},{"he":"אַף אֶחָד לֹא בָּא.","en":"Nobody came."},{"he":"אַף פַּעַם לֹא הָיִיתִי שָׁם.","en":"I've never been there."}]},{"type":"tip","body":"Hebrew doubles its negatives and means it. אַף אֶחָד לֹא בָּא is literally nobody didn't come, and means nobody came. Dropping the לֹא is wrong."}],"vocab":[{"he":"לֹא","en":"no, not","translit":"lo"},{"he":"אַף אֶחָד","en":"nobody","translit":"af echad"},{"he":"אַף פַּעַם","en":"never","translit":"af pa'am"},{"he":"כְּלוּם","en":"nothing","translit":"klum"},{"he":"עֲדַיִן לֹא","en":"not yet","translit":"adayin lo"},{"he":"רַק","en":"only","translit":"rak"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["is finished","door","no, not","to him"],"correct":2,"prompt":"לֹא","translit":"lo"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["a little","nobody","children","of"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אַף אֶחָד","translit":"af echad"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["holiday","nevertheless","land, country","never"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אַף פַּעַם","translit":"af pa'am"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["nothing","house","fish","teaches"],"correct":0,"prompt":"כְּלוּם","translit":"klum"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["come! (f.)","not yet","sister","his name"],"correct":1,"prompt":"עֲדַיִן לֹא","translit":"adayin lo"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["writes","only","grandfather","coffee"],"correct":1,"prompt":"רַק","translit":"rak"},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["כְּלוּם","רַק","אַף אֶחָד","עֲדַיִן לֹא"],"correct":3,"say":"עֲדַיִן לֹא","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “never”?","options":["אוֹר","מַכִּיר","אַף פַּעַם","אַל"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"רַק","translit":"rak","en":"only"},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["אַף אֶחָד","אַף פַּעַם","לֹא","רַק"],"correct":1,"say":"אַף פַּעַם","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “nobody”?","options":["לָלֶכֶת","אָחוֹת","עָלַי","אַף אֶחָד"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["רַק","כְּלוּם","עֲדַיִן לֹא","אַף אֶחָד"],"correct":3,"say":"אַף אֶחָד","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “only”?","options":["רַק","בְּוַדַּאי","מִי","הַחוּצָה"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “not yet”?","options":["יַלְדָּה","מֶלֶךְ","אִישׁ","עֲדַיִן לֹא"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["אַף אֶחָד","nobody"],["אַף פַּעַם","never"],["לֹא","no, not"],["עֲדַיִן לֹא","not yet"],["רַק","only"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"“Nobody came” —","options":["אַף אֶחָד לֹא בָּא","אַף אֶחָד בָּא","לֹא אַף אֶחָד בָּא","אֵין אֶחָד בָּא"],"correct":0,"why":"The negative word and לֹא both appear; Hebrew requires the double negative."}]}